    "body": "## Result\n\nOwner-requested expert comparison of the complete two-page XOR/Hamming document against native source and the current protected-direction blocker. Retain its valid Boolean definitions and typed contract ideas; no new mechanism adoption or language gain. Existing geometry-bound Hamming already covers much of the proposal. The retained H4 census gives antipodal distance90/120, so bitwise complement is not geometric negation in that encoding. The proposed path/routing predicates do not establish icosian composition or optimal routing.\n\nThe source-linked report recommends reusing existing typed implementations and continuing protected-constraint-aware joint direction formation. Accepted8/512 and all milestone statuses remain unchanged. No model, Lean/Rust build, or scoring executed.\n\n## Validation at `654ef81b5690328d0ef905f40afbaf852f19fa1b`\n\nParent exact-head review of the full specialist report, both PDF pages and relevant source/evidence; PDF hash verified; all22 pinned repository paths/line anchors resolve; claim wording and diff whitespace pass. Only two Markdown files changed. Queue acknowledgements execute no tests.\n\n- [x] Dated research record with artifact identity, scope, decision and limitations\n- [x] Newest-first current-state entry ending in Next\n- [x] Existing Hamming/identity documents searched; no changed capability or stale implementation claim\n- [x] README/STATUS/ROADMAP/tracker unchanged: no capability, mechanism or milestone change\n- [x] Exact-head review and applicable checks complete\n- [x] After merge: verify fresh main, delete branch/worktree, preserve review material, apply hygiene and report on M2\n\nReferences #2030\n",
